// Title: Potential Persistence Via Microsoft Compatibility Appraiser
// Sigma ID: f548a603-c9f2-4c89-b511-b089f7e94549
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Sreeman
// Date: 2020-09-29 | Modified: 2023-02-10
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, execution, persistence, T1053.005
// Description: Detects manual execution of the "Microsoft Compatibility Appraiser" task via schtasks. In order
//   to trigger persistence stored in the "\AppCompatFlags\TelemetryController" registry key.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.trustedsec.com/blog/abusing-windows-telemetry-for-persistence/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_schtasks_persistence_windows_telemetry.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\schtasks.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "schtasks.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "run " and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Application Experience\\Microsoft Compatibility Appraiser")
